    "advancement": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>2nd-level Shadow feature</em></p><p>You can expend one use of Devotion and enshroud your body in shadow energy as a bonus action. For one minute, you gain the following effects:</p><ul><li><p>You can't cast spells that restore hit points, unless it is one of your Shadow Calling spells.</p></li><li><p>You have advantage on Charisma (Intimidation) and Dexterity (Stealth) checks, but disadvantage on all other Charisma checks.</p></li><li><p>Once per turn, when you hit a creature with an attack, or when a creature fails a saving throw from one of your priest spells, you can invoke primal fear in them. The target must succeed on a Charisma saving throw or become frightened of you for 1 minute. The frightened target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p></li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a short of long rest, unless you spend two uses of Devotion to use it again.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
